  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Two basketball players take turns shooting, with success probabilities $p$ and $r$ respectively, until one makes a basket and wins.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q29-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If the player with probability $p$ shoots first, find the probability that they win.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{p}{1-(1-p)(1-r)}$.\n\nIf both players miss, the competition resets.",
          "worked": "Let $w$ be the probability that the first player wins. They either score immediately or both players miss and the competition resets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}w&=p+(1-p)(1-r)w\\\\w\\bigl[1-(1-p)(1-r)\\bigr]&=p\\\\w&=\\frac{p}{1-(1-p)(1-r)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q29-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the condition on $p$ and $r$ so that both players have an equal chance of winning.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=\\dfrac{r}{1+r}$.\n\nSet the first player's winning probability equal to $\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "For equal chances, each player's winning probability is $\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{p}{1-(1-p)(1-r)}&=\\frac12\\\\2p&=1-(1-p)(1-r)\\\\2p&=p+r-pr\\\\p(1+r)&=r\\\\p&=\\frac{r}{1+r}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      }
    ]
  },
